{
  "title": "Discussion on AI tools, job search, and code generation",
  "topics": [
    {
      "id": "ai-job-search",
      "title": "Using AI for job search and application preparation",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The author is preparing for a full‑time job search and plans to set up cloud automation for generating PDF resumes tailored to specific vacancies.",
          "evidence": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "They intend to configure OpenClaw to find vacancies, generate resumes, and write cover letters once their startup is closed.",
          "evidence": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "In 2026, adding many AI‑related skills (Cursor, Claude Code, LLM, RAG, embeddings, etc.) is necessary to avoid being filtered out by recruiters.",
          "evidence": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "AI has become a market mainstream, and lacking AI knowledge makes job search for JS/Python positions very difficult.",
          "evidence": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The acceleration of development due to AI tools became significant only around 2025, despite earlier theories from 2022.",
          "evidence": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The author expects the recruiter profession to disappear, leaving HR as a personnel management role.",
          "evidence": [14]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-code-generation",
      "title": "Problems with AI‑generated code and performance",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "AI‑generated raw SQL (450 lines) pulled almost all data from the database, leading to unoptimized queries that could take 10–20 minutes in production.",
          "evidence": [30]
        },
        {
          "text": "Incremental computations have been replaced by a view, suggesting a shift in data handling architecture.",
          "evidence": [34]
        },
        {
          "text": "A developer used AI to generate code that broke the project; after review the team decided to drop the feature entirely because the code was inadequate.",
          "evidence": [35]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recruiter-role",
      "title": "Changing relevance of recruiters",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Candidate search via keyword tags is becoming more detached from reality than before.",
          "evidence": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "The author predicts the recruiter profession will become extinct, with HR focusing on personnel management.",
          "evidence": [14]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "development-acceleration",
      "title": "AI speeding up development workflows",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Using GPT to generate code for joining tables accelerates development by handling routine tasks, allowing developers to focus on higher‑level problems.",
          "evidence": [19]
        },
        {
          "text": "The author notes that while AI speeds up coding, their projects lack cloud infrastructure and likely never will.",
          "evidence": [19]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
